WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.594
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.894 --> 00:00:09.849
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.149 --> 00:00:19.234
Unit six: B1 Preliminary: Overview and Reading Parts. Today you will understand the B1 Preliminary exam and the six Reading parts.

4
00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:22.221
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.574
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:28.348
Preliminary.

7
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.580
Preliminary means coming before the main test (the exam name).

8
00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:35.647
B1 Preliminary is also called PET.

9
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.042
Your turn. Say: Preliminary.

10
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:42.913
Preliminary.

11
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.396
Gist.

12
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:47.186
Gist means the general meaning.

13
00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:49.133
Read for the gist.

14
00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:51.707
Your turn. Say: Gist.

15
00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:55.475
Gist.

16
00:00:56.217 --> 00:00:57.578
Advertisement.

17
00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:01.326
Advertisement means a message that sells something.

18
00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:03.777
Match the people to adverts.

19
00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:07.384
Your turn. Say: Advertisement.

20
00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:11.258
Advertisement.

21
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:12.948
Opinion.

22
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.984
Opinion means what someone thinks.

23
00:01:16.583 --> 00:01:18.339
The writer gives an opinion.

24
00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.544
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

25
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.401
Opinion.

26
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.139
Attitude.

27
00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.556
Attitude means how someone feels.

28
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.906
What is the writer's attitude?

29
00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:35.890
Your turn. Say: Attitude.

30
00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:39.700
Attitude.

31
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.230
Gap.

32
00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:43.833
Gap means a missing part.

33
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:45.929
Fill the gap with a word.

34
00:01:46.517 --> 00:01:48.902
Your turn. Say: Gap.

35
00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:52.466
Gap.

36
00:01:53.217 --> 00:01:54.717
Multiple choice.

37
00:01:55.717 --> 00:01:58.831
Multiple choice means a question with several options.

38
00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:01.625
Answer the multiple-choice questions.

39
00:02:02.217 --> 00:02:05.345
Your turn. Say: Multiple choice.

40
00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.700
Multiple choice.

41
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:11.335
Cloze.

42
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.605
Cloze means a text with missing words.

43
00:02:15.217 --> 00:02:16.880
Part 5 is a cloze.

44
00:02:17.483 --> 00:02:20.136
Your turn. Say: Cloze.

45
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:23.966
Cloze.

46
00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:28.696
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.281
Visal, what is B1 Preliminary?

48
00:02:33.383 --> 00:02:46.194
It is a Cambridge exam for intermediate English. It has Reading, Writing, Listening and Speaking, and it shows that you can deal with everyday situations and simple texts.

49
00:02:47.283 --> 00:02:49.294
How is the Reading paper organised?

50
00:02:50.383 --> 00:03:05.131
There are six parts: signs and messages, matching people to texts, a longer text with questions on opinions, a text with missing sentences, a multiple-choice cloze and an open cloze.

51
00:03:06.217 --> 00:03:08.414
What is the best general strategy?

52
00:03:09.517 --> 00:03:20.099
Read the instructions, skim the text for the gist, then read the questions and look for exact answers. Check that every detail of your answer matches the text.

53
00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:22.850
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:23.683 --> 00:03:27.749
Grammar focus: Strategy: gist first, then detail.

55
00:03:28.049 --> 00:03:29.260
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.681
I skim the text to understand the general idea.

57
00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:36.419
Then I find evidence for each answer in the text.

58
00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:45.093
Skim for the gist, read each question carefully and find evidence in the text. Do not choose an answer just because it looks familiar.

59
00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:49.617
Be careful! Don't say: I read every word first.

60
00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:54.077
Say: I skim for the gist first.

61
00:03:54.377 --> 00:03:55.459
Gist first.

62
00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.780
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:00.870
Reading Strategy.

64
00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.761
Visal studies for B1 Preliminary.

65
00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:08.322
He first reads the instructions to see what each part asks.

66
00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:11.751
He skims the text for the general idea.

67
00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:15.997
Then he reads the questions and finds evidence in the text.

68
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.615
He checks that his answer fits every detail.

69
00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.713
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.629
How many Reading parts does B1 Preliminary have?

71
00:04:28.929 --> 00:04:31.956
A, six. B, two. C, ten.

72
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.302
The answer is A: six.

73
00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.974
The gist is the blank.

74
00:04:40.274 --> 00:04:44.159
A, price. B, general meaning. C, spelling.

75
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.025
The answer is B: general meaning.

76
00:04:51.183 --> 00:04:52.835
A cloze text has blank.

77
00:04:53.135 --> 00:04:57.090
A, no words. B, pictures only. C, missing words.

78
00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.737
The answer is C: missing words.

79
00:05:03.883 --> 00:05:05.674
Visal first reads the blank.

80
00:05:05.974 --> 00:05:09.836
A, instructions. B, answers. C, dictionary.

81
00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.562
The answer is A: instructions.

82
00:05:16.717 --> 00:05:18.356
Your answer must fit blank.

83
00:05:18.656 --> 00:05:23.134
A, the title only. B, every detail. C, one word.

84
00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.036
The answer is B: every detail.

85
00:05:30.233 --> 00:05:33.501
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.419
How do you prepare for the Reading paper?

87
00:05:45.217 --> 00:05:46.787
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:47.087 --> 00:05:59.680
I read the instructions for each part and practise skimming for the gist. Then I read the questions and look for evidence in the text. I check that my answer matches every detail before I move on.

89
00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:01.979
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:02.883 --> 00:06:08.438
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: gist first, then detail.

91
00:06:08.738 --> 00:06:13.248
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:06:13.548 --> 00:06:16.015
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:16.315 --> 00:06:19.431
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

